REFERENCE   1
  CONSRTM   Wellcome Sanger Tree of Life Programme
  TITLE     Direct Submission
  JOURNAL   Submitted (20-JUL-2022) WELLCOME SANGER INSTITUTE, Tree of Life,
            Wellcome Genome Campus, Hinxton CB10 1SA, United Kingdom
COMMENT     The assembly wcLumRube1.1 is based on 30x PacBio data, 10X Genomics
            Chromium data, and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of
            Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly
            process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio
            assembly generation with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with
            purge_dups, short-read polishing using FreeBayes-called variants
            from 10X Genomics Chromium reads aligned with LongRanger, and Hi-C
            based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled
            using MitoHiFi. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and
            manually improved using rapid curation. Chromosome-scale scaffolds
            confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size.
